Also when paused, still animate.

Swing trigger: in breakBlock & placeBlock: `this.swingPhase = 0;`. Also maybe on mouse down even if miss? Minecraft swings on click. Call in onCanvasMouseDown for left/right. But breakBlock may fail; still animate. Add `this.swingPhase = 0` in mouse handlers before break/place. Also touch break/place. Simplest: add `this.swingHand()` in breakBlock at start and placeBlock at start.

Select updates held block texture: in `select()`, call `this.updateHandBlock()`.

```js
updateHandBlock() {
  if (!this.handBlockMat) return;
  const tex = makeBlockTexture(this.hotbar[this.selected].tile);
  const old = this.handBlockMat.map;
  this.handBlockMat.map = tex;
  this.handBlockMat.needsUpdate = true;
  old?.dispose();
}
```
Always show held block. Good.

Night vision: in setupScene toggle class. On dispose remove.

Mods speed:
```
const boost = this.mods.rabbitBoots ? 1.4 : 1;
const speed = (p.fly ? 10.5 : ...) * boost;
```
Fly speed perhaps also boosted; fine.
Jump: `p.vel.y = 8.4 * (this.mods.slimeJump ? 1.3 : 1)`.

Reach: replace raycast(6) occurrences (updateHighlight, breakBlock, placeBlock) with this.reach.

Emerald on break: `this.app.addEmeralds?.(1);` after stats.broken++.

Dispose arm: remove from camera and dispose group geometries/materials/maps.

Add a small method `disposeHand()`.

Also note `this.viewer.scene.add(camera)` is needed; add each game. In dispose, don't remove camera (harmless). But if camera has arm removed, fine. Also stopGame sets viewer.setWorld(panoWorld) with camera still in scene at old position; menu loop camera position updates. Fine.

Constructor ordering: this.mods, this.reach before setupScene. Also this.swingPhase = 1; this.handTime = 0.

